media: rkisp1: support RK3288, and sensors on the low lines of the bus

The ISP of the RK3288 is the same V10 block as the RK3399's. Add it,
with its pixel input and JPEG/second core clocks, and without the MIPI
receiver, which needs a D-PHY driver.

The parallel input is MSB aligned: in the 8 and 10-bit modes the samples
come from the top lines of the 12-line bus. On the Archos 101 Oxygen the
OV5640's 8 data lines go to the ISP's D7-D0 instead. Read such a sensor
at the endpoint's full bus-width, and scale the samples back up with the
sensor de-gamma curve by default; userspace parameters can still
replace that curve.

On 32-bit ARM the IOMMU DMA mapping code splits imported buffers into
segments of the device's maximum size (64 KiB by default) placed anywhere
in the address space, and vb2-dma-contig then rejects them. Allow a single
segment.

